      "outputTokens": 712,
      "costUsd": 0.0064564999999999996,
      "pronunciationText": "That value is called the limiting sum, S infinity. It's the number the totals get closer and closer to, as we add more and more terms. So S infinity equals a over one minus r. For our series, it's sixty-four over a half, which is one hundred and twenty-eight. But it only works when r is between minus one and one. That's often written with the size of r, mod r, less than one."
    },
