      "inputTokens": 97,
      "outputTokens": 626,
      "costUsd": 0.0056825,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the ball's whole journey. It falls one hundred and twenty-eight centimetres. After that, every bounce goes up and comes back down the same height, so each bounce height is travelled twice. Those heights have a limiting sum of one hundred and twenty-eight. So the ball travels one hundred and twenty-eight, plus two times one hundred and twenty-eight, which is three hundred and eighty-four centimetres. Infinitely many bounces, but a finite distance."
    },
