      "inputTokens": 118,
      "outputTokens": 898,
      "costUsd": 0.008141,
      "pronunciationText": "When r is negative, the totals zigzag. Take eight, minus four, plus two, minus one, and so on. Here r is minus a half. The totals go eight, four, six, five, five and a half, jumping above and below one value, and closing in. S infinity is eight, over one minus minus a half. That's eight over three halves, which is sixteen thirds, about five point three three. Here the first term is positive, and a negative r adds to the bottom, so the limiting sum is smaller than the first term."
    },
