      "inputTokens": 113,
      "outputTokens": 849,
      "costUsd": 0.0076975,
      "pronunciationText": "Limiting sums also turn repeating decimals into fractions. Zero point two seven two seven, repeating, is twenty-seven hundredths, plus twenty-seven ten-thousandths, and so on. Each piece is one hundredth of the one before, so r is one hundredth. Then S infinity is twenty-seven hundredths, over ninety-nine hundredths. The hundredths cancel, leaving twenty-seven over ninety-nine, which simplifies to three elevenths. Check: three divided by eleven is zero point two seven two seven, repeating."
