      "costUsd": 0.0053405,
      "pronunciationText": "Here ay is ten, so ten over one minus r equals forty. Then one minus r is ten over forty, which is a quarter, so r is three quarters. Check the condition: three quarters is between minus one and one, so this limiting sum exists. Minus three is wrong. It turns the fraction upside down, and a ratio of minus three has no limiting sum at all."
