      "costUsd": 0.0057599999999999995,
      "pronunciationText": "First find the ratio. Each term is two x times the one before, so r is two x. A limiting sum needs the size of two x to be less than one. So two x is between minus one and one, and x is between minus a half and a half. Then S infinity is one over one minus two x. Minus one to one is wrong. The condition is on the ratio, two x, not on x."
